Hi,

To patch, you can do
$ cd /usr/src/linux-2.6
$ patch -p1 -i /some/where/ZFx86.patch

I think, you want to enabel gx-suspmod feature as module,
you may set
CPU Frequency scaling = module
Cyrix MediaGX/NatSemi Geode Suspend Modulation = module

A reboot behavior is not my patch issue.
I did not touch the boot related code.

Do you set cpufreq modules as build into kernel?
A gx-suspmod driver causes reboot?

